WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.103
Here's an illustrative design, not a
validated configuration, for an agency

2
00:00:05.103 --> 00:00:10.075
that owns ten dot zero slash eight and
example dot gov, with four divisions.

3
00:00:10.075 --> 00:00:13.088
Headquarters is the central
network operations team.

4
00:00:13.088 --> 00:00:17.388
It holds its own slash-twelve block
and its own zone under pattern A,

5
00:00:17.388 --> 00:00:21.688
and it hosts the central superusers
and a read-only approver group.

6
00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:23.459
If example dot gov is signed,

7
00:00:23.459 --> 00:00:27.000
the central management node
signs it as hidden primary.

8
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.088
The law-enforcement bureau needs
confidentiality from the other divisions.

9
00:00:31.088 --> 00:00:35.561
It gets its own block and its own
zone, served from its own two servers,

10
00:00:35.561 --> 00:00:40.275
patterns A and B, and nothing else,
because everything else stays denied.

11
00:00:40.275 --> 00:00:42.625
Its data stays out of shared dashboards.

12
00:00:42.625 --> 00:00:46.124
If its change detail shouldn't
reach headquarters approvers,

13
00:00:46.124 --> 00:00:48.937
a bureau-lead approver
group can own its workflow.

14
00:00:48.937 --> 00:00:53.688
The regional office still
runs Windows DNS and DHCP.

15
00:00:53.688 --> 00:00:59.177
The platform manages those servers, and the
region's group gets rights on them only,

16
00:00:59.177 --> 00:01:03.051
never the platform-wide DNS
and DHCP administrator roles.

17
00:01:03.051 --> 00:01:06.188
Each server's network view
is fixed at first sync.

18
00:01:06.188 --> 00:01:10.488
The research lab numbered itself in
a range that overlaps headquarters.

19
00:01:10.488 --> 00:01:15.189
It gets its own network view or
IP space and its own DHCP pair,

20
00:01:15.189 --> 00:01:20.562
pattern C, and its zone is delegated
to lab-run BIND servers, pattern D.

21
00:01:20.562 --> 00:01:24.174
The lab hands central the DS
records for its signed zone,

22
00:01:24.174 --> 00:01:28.700
and federation records its space as
an overlapping block behind NAT.
